course: dictionary
lesson: 12195
title: Word meanings: confine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confine is a verb, and it has more than one meaning. The sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. Look for clues like small spaces, limits, illness or rules. «The dog was confined to the kitchen.» The kitchen is a small space, so confined means kept inside that space and not allowed into the rest of the house.
explain: Confine can also mean keep something within a limit, so it does not spread or go beyond. «Please confine your answer to 100 words.» Nobody is putting your answer in a cage. The clue is the number: you must stop at 100 words. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence instead of the hard word.
explain: You can also be confined to bed when you are very ill or hurt. «Ben had a broken leg, so he was confined to bed for two weeks.» Broken leg and bed are the clues. Swap in your meaning: "Ben had to stay in bed" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Confine means to keep someone or something inside a small or closed space.
fact: Confine also means to keep something within a limit, so it does not spread or go beyond it.
fact: «Confined to bed» means you have to stay in bed, usually because of illness or injury.
fact: A «confined space» is a small space with little room to move.
fact: Old-fashioned use: to be confined can mean to be in bed to give birth to a baby. You may see this in old stories.
exercise: «The fire was confined to one room.» What does confined mean here? | *Kept inside one place and not spreading | Spread out across the whole house | Painted a bright colour | Put out by the rain
exercise: «Please confine your answer to the question.» What does confine mean here? | Write the answer twice | Write the answer in a cage | *Keep it within the topic and do not go beyond it | Forget the question
exercise: «Ben had a broken leg, so he was confined to bed for two weeks.» Find and copy one word that tells you why. | Ben | *broken | weeks | confined
test: «The puppy was confined to the garden while we cleaned the house.» What does confined mean here? | Taken for a long walk | *Kept inside the garden | Let run free everywhere | Given a new bed
test: What does «confined to bed» mean? | Hiding under the bed | *Having to stay in bed, usually because of illness or injury | Sleeping very well all night | Making the bed neatly
exam: Jayden asks, «Does confine always mean put in a cage?» What is the answer? | No, it means to shout loudly | *No, it can also mean keep something within a limit, like a word count | No, it means to forget | Yes, it always means put in a cage
